id:                     E2166
trigger_tool:           cmake|clang|conan
phase:                  compilation
error_signature:        GLOB_BRACE.*undeclared|use of undeclared identifier 'GLOB_BRACE'
severity:               2
category:               libc|posix-portability|cmake
match_keywords:         glob.h, GLOB_BRACE, GLOB_TILDE, musl, CVD_INTERNAL_GLOB_IS_BAD
title:                  Prefer an upstream plain-glob fallback when GNU glob flags are unavailable
root_cause:             A project may detect glob() and still unconditionally compile GNU-only GLOB_BRACE or GLOB_TILDE. OpenHarmony's musl headers provide glob() without those extensions, so the feature check passes but compilation fails.
affected_scope:         C/C++ projects that check only glob() availability and subsequently use nonportable glob flags, provided an existing zero-flags fallback is present.
verification_cmd:       Configure libcvd with CVD_INTERNAL_GLOB_IS_BAD=ON; compile on OHOS arm64; run ctest --output-on-failure -j1 (5/5) and the Conan consumer test.
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           enable-upstream-glob-fallback
rec_description:        Inspect the upstream code for an existing flag-free glob path. Enable it via the project's own CMake option, preserving upstream source and testing the resulting behavior on the target.
rec_command:            CMakeToolchain(self).cache_variables["CVD_INTERNAL_GLOB_IS_BAD"] = True
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-cmake-option
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      guard-nonportable-glob-flags
fallback_description:   Only if no upstream fallback exists, guard each extension flag with its actual preprocessor symbol and separately test affected pathname semantics.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:
forbid_1_pattern:       define GLOB_BRACE 0|define GLOB_TILDE 0
forbid_1_reason:        A blind macro replacement changes brace or tilde expansion semantics without an explicit portability decision.
forbid_1_consequence:   Builds may pass while file matching behaves differently.
principles:             P005,P013
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []
doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/E2166-draft-2501.md
last_updated:           2026-09-24
source_event:           libcvd 30e8cfc on HarmonyOS PC arm64; original build failed in cvd_src/globlist.cxx at GLOB_BRACE; upstream fallback enabled and full JPEG/PNG/TIFF build passed all five enabled CTest tests plus Conan test_package.
metrics_success_count:  1
metrics_fail_count:     1
metrics_confidence:     0.9
draft:                  true
contributor_id:         2501_91199785
